 **Progressive disclosure** — root context files point; they do not inline. A line that says "read X for Y" costs ~10–15 tokens and stays accurate indefinitely. Inlined content costs hundreds of tokens and drifts the moment the source is updated.
 
-**Length budget** — root context files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, steering files): 60–130 lines. Engineering Guide articles: under 150 lines. LLD container docs: under 120 lines. HLD container docs: under 80 lines. If essential detail exceeds the budget, split a focused companion document and link it; never replace missing coverage with compressed, unreadable prose.
+**Length budget** — measured in prose lines only: Mermaid diagram blocks and tables never count against it, however long, since they carry information density prose can't match. Root context files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, steering files): 60–130 lines. Engineering Guide articles: under 150 lines. LLD container docs: under 120 lines. HLD container docs: under 80 lines. When prose still doesn't fit and the remaining content is genuinely essential, split a focused companion document along the natural topic boundary and link it — do this readily, not as a last resort fought over line-by-line; never compress essential coverage into dense, unreadable prose to stay under budget.
 
 **Certainty principle** — architecture docs (HLD, LLD, NFR) state only settled outcomes. No unresolved comparisons or open questions, and no Gaps, open-question or TODO placeholder sections — including empty "no gaps" declarations. Keep uncertainty in the external run, design or review record (`Stories/<TICKET>/design/`). State approved targets separately from observed behavior; include rationale only when a decision source supports it. → See `docs/README.md`.
 
